WEBVTT

NOTE Converted from Tech-Adoption-Radar-for-Confluence.srt (= demo-video-funny-master-captions-v2.srt).
NOTE Cue setting shifts every caption right of centre so the "Excuses" quadrant label (x 31-35%, y 83%) stays visible.

1
00:00:00.156 --> 00:00:03.866 position:62% align:center size:50%
At Cloudscript, we know guidance only works
when people actually read it.

2
00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:06.586 position:62% align:center size:50%
So we built Tech Adoption
Radar for Confluence -

3
00:00:06.936 --> 00:00:10.326 position:62% align:center size:50%
so your radar lives with the documentation
your team already uses.

4
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.490 position:62% align:center size:50%
This is our team's adoption radar.

5
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.890 position:62% align:center size:50%
Four quadrants, four rings.

6
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.200 position:62% align:center size:50%
Everything we're adopting,
trialling, assessing -

7
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.390 position:62% align:center size:50%
in a place where we know
people will look at it.

8
00:00:24.296 --> 00:00:26.386 position:62% align:center size:50%
Adding one is a slash command away.

9
00:00:26.576 --> 00:00:28.536 position:62% align:center size:50%
Type your blips straight into the table,

10
00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:31.760 position:62% align:center size:50%
paste them from the spreadsheet
you already keep,

11
00:00:33.686 --> 00:00:37.856 position:62% align:center size:50%
or upload a CSV or radar.js JSON file.

12
00:00:38.826 --> 00:00:42.136 position:62% align:center size:50%
Same list, any route, same radar.

13
00:00:42.605 --> 00:00:44.495 position:62% align:center size:50%
The blip shapes tell you what moved.

14
00:00:44.905 --> 00:00:47.765 position:62% align:center size:50%
Synergies moved out - some time ago.

15
00:00:48.525 --> 00:00:49.975 position:62% align:center size:50%
Multi-modal just moved in.

16
00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:54.215 position:62% align:center size:50%
And new arrivals get a star,
like this quarter's newest entry.

17
00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:57.999 position:62% align:center size:50%
When something moves, you edit one line.

18
00:00:58.099 --> 00:00:59.719 position:62% align:center size:50%
The blip moves, with a marker -

19
00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:02.479 position:62% align:center size:50%
and the change lands in page history,

20
00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.559 position:62% align:center size:50%
so the radar has an audit trail.

21
00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.559 position:62% align:center size:50%
For example: last sprint,

22
00:01:07.639 --> 00:01:09.679 position:62% align:center size:50%
"Ask how the integration project is going"

23
00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.199 position:62% align:center size:50%
moved from Adopt... to Hold.

24
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.840 position:62% align:center size:50%
Blips link to your own pages.

25
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.408 position:62% align:center size:50%
Let's see how the
integration project is going.

26
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.418 position:62% align:center size:50%
Note the page links
straight back to the radar.

27
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:27.699 position:62% align:center size:50%
Need the image for a slide deck?

28
00:01:28.319 --> 00:01:30.271 position:62% align:center size:50%
One click - it's right here on the radar.

29
00:01:30.698 --> 00:01:32.618 position:62% align:center size:50%
Confluence's page exports work too.

30
00:01:33.547 --> 00:01:35.728 position:62% align:center size:50%
PDF captures the radar as you see it.

31
00:01:36.378 --> 00:01:39.008 position:62% align:center size:50%
If the descriptions matter, Word export
provides them -

32
00:01:39.088 --> 00:01:40.718 position:62% align:center size:50%
every blip, in a table.

33
00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.806 position:62% align:center size:50%
Tech Adoption Radar for Confluence,
on the Atlassian Marketplace.

34
00:01:47.986 --> 00:01:50.605 position:62% align:center size:50%
So there's no excuse for not knowing
what's acceptable.

35
00:01:51.265 --> 00:01:53.805 position:62% align:center size:50%
Oh - and you can use
it for technology too.
